# NOTE: a _redirects rule can NEVER hide a file that exists. Cloudflare Pages serves
# static assets BEFORE consulting this file, so a "/docs/* -> 404" rule silently does
# nothing and the file is served anyway (verified in production, 2026-07-17).
# The publish root IS the repo root: anything committed here is public. Internal docs
# therefore live outside the repo (../website-internal-docs/), not behind a rule.
# Sales OS is its own app under /sales/. It needs NO rule: static assets win over the
# /* fallback on their own. A self-referential "/sales/* -> /sales/:splat 200" rewrite
# lived here and broke it - Pages resolved the no-op rewrite, found nothing, and fell
# through to /* -> /index.html, so every sales asset returned the marketing homepage as
# text/html. The page rendered unstyled with no nav (verified in production, 2026-08-07).
# E7: canonicalize duplicate topic URLs to their richer dedicated landing pages
/industry/environmental-remediation    /environmental-remediation-solutions    301
/industry/distributors    /distributors-resellers-industries    301
# Shopify commerce paths must NEVER reach the SPA fallback below. Post-cutover the apex
# serves this site, so a stale /cart/<variant>:<qty> permalink would match /* and render
# the homepage with a 200 - a broken checkout that looks like a working page and shows up
# in no error log (verified 2026-08-06). Bounce them to the store instead.
# These MUST stay above the /* fallback; _redirects matches top-down, first rule wins.
# Requires shop.americanbiocarbon.com to be Shopify's PRIMARY domain - if the apex is
# still primary, Shopify 301s back here and the two rules form an infinite loop.
/cart           https://shop.americanbiocarbon.com/cart              302
/cart/*         https://shop.americanbiocarbon.com/cart/:splat       302
/checkouts/*    https://shop.americanbiocarbon.com/checkouts/:splat  302
/checkout       https://shop.americanbiocarbon.com/checkout          302
# Marketing site hash-router SPA fallback
/*    /index.html    200
